   "id": "I181",
   "why": "Skeletons storming the earliest print-shop woodcut, captioned 'Deadline': a striking archive engraving plus a one-word caption that reframes it. Exactly the shop's best-selling formula, and funny to anyone."
  },
  {
   "id": "I186",
   "why": "Engraved monk with a real scribal colophon: 'For Christ's sake, give me a drink.' Strong image, a laugh that anyone gets, and an easy pub-shirt conversation starter."
  },
  {
   "id": "I178",
   "why": "The Ea-nasir complaint tablet is already a beloved internet meme. The cuneiform makes a handsome one-ink texture, and the caption lands on its own."
  },
